IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cema-types`

-- Customs and Excise Management Act 1979 (UK) — GOAL 2: PENALTIES FOR
-- FRAUDULENT EVASION (ss 149(1), 170, Schedule 1).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1979-2.txt.

§ `Goal 2 — penalties for fraudulent evasion`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` a b MEANS IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

-- s 170(1): knowingly acquiring or dealing with goods (unlawfully removed
-- from a warehouse, chargeable with unpaid duty, or subject to a prohibition
-- or restriction) with intent to defraud of duty or evade the prohibition;
-- (2): being knowingly concerned in a fraudulent evasion or attempt. (5): not
-- where a corresponding offence with its own penalty applies.
@ref s 170(1), (2), (5)
@export Whether an offence under s 170 of the Customs and Excise Management Act 1979 (UK) is made out: knowingly acquiring or dealing with goods with intent to defraud of duty or evade a prohibition or restriction (s 170(1)), or being knowingly concerned in a fraudulent evasion or attempt (s 170(2)); not where a corresponding offence with its own penalty applies (s 170(5)). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN e IS AN `Evasion facts`  @desc The conduct, knowledge and intent, and whether a corresponding offence applies
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under s 170 is made out by` e IF
        (   (e's `knowingly acquired or dealt with the goods` AND e's `with intent to defraud of duty or evade a prohibition`)
         OR e's `knowingly concerned in a fraudulent evasion or attempt`)
    AND NOT (e's `a corresponding offence with its own penalty applies`)

DECLARE `Maximum term` IS ONE OF
    `imprisonment for life`
    `imprisonment for months` HAS `months` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Maximum penalties` HAS
    `summary penalty`                                   IS A NUMBER
    `summary imprisonment, months`                      IS A NUMBER
    -- NOTHING: "a penalty of any amount".
    `penalty on indictment`                             IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `imprisonment on indictment`                        IS A `Maximum term`

-- s 170(3) "(a) on summary conviction, to a penalty of the prescribed sum
-- [£20,000] or of three times the value of the goods, whichever is the
-- greater, or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months ...; (b) on
-- conviction on indictment, to a penalty of any amount, or to imprisonment
-- for a term not exceeding 14 years". Sch 1: Class A, life; Class B or
-- temporary class, 14 years; Class C, summary "three times the value of the
-- goods or £500, whichever is the greater, or ... 3 months", indictment 14
-- years. (4A): the listed weapons, life on indictment. (4B): seal skins,
-- summary "a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum [£20,000] or ...
-- three months", indictment 2 years.
@ref s 170(3)-(4B), Sch 1
@export The maximum penalties for an offence under s 170 of the Customs and Excise Management Act 1979 (UK), by kind of goods: on summary conviction the greater of the fixed sum and three times the value (Class C: the greater of three times the value and £500; seal skins: the fixed sum alone), with 6 months (Class C and seal skins: 3 months); on indictment a penalty of any amount, with 14 years (Class A drugs and s 170(4A) weapons: life; seal skins: 2 years). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN e IS AN `Evasion facts`  @desc The kind of goods, their value, and the summary fixed sum
GIVETH A `Maximum penalties`
`the maximum penalties under s 170 for` e MEANS
    CONSIDER e's `kind of goods`
    WHEN `a Class A drug` THEN
        `Maximum penalties` OF standardSummary, 6, NOTHING, `imprisonment for life`
    WHEN `a Class C drug` THEN
        `Maximum penalties` OF (`the greater of` threeTimes 500), 3, NOTHING, `imprisonment for months` 168
    WHEN `a prohibited weapon within s 170(4A)` THEN
        `Maximum penalties` OF standardSummary, 6, NOTHING, `imprisonment for life`
    WHEN `seal skins` THEN
        `Maximum penalties` OF (e's `the summary fixed sum`), 3, NOTHING, `imprisonment for months` 24
    OTHERWISE
        `Maximum penalties` OF standardSummary, 6, NOTHING, `imprisonment for months` 168
    WHERE
        threeTimes MEANS 3 TIMES e's `value of the goods`
        standardSummary MEANS `the greater of` (e's `the summary fixed sum`) threeTimes

-- s 149(1): in England and Wales (magistrates' court) or Scotland (court of
-- summary jurisdiction), the aggregate of imprisonment for the offence and
-- for non-payment of the penalty "shall not exceed 15 months".
@ref s 149(1), (3)
`the maximum aggregate imprisonment on summary conviction and default, months` MEANS 15
